From: pletch <17855860+pletch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:36:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dummynet_st: CAKE's targets from the release interval

The third of the sub-tick release series (opnsense-cake SUBTICK.md).
CAKE raises a tin's target to at least 1.5 times DN_RELEASE_GRAIN_NS,
the tick on a stock dummynet (15 ms at kern.hz=100), because packets
leave in batches that far apart. Here they are release_us apart, so
the target need not grow beyond 1.5 times that. The targets are set when
a pipe is configured, so release_us should be set before.
---
 sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_private.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_private.h b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_private.h
index 13ddfe05115..dd156df7c9e 100644
--- a/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_private.h
+++ b/sys/netpfil/ipfw/ip_dn_private.h
@@ -101,6 +101,9 @@ set_oid(struct dn_id *o, int type, int len)
  */
 #define DN_CREDIT_HZ	1000000
 #define DN_RELEASE_NS	((uint64_t)dn_release() * 1000)
+/* CAKE widens its targets to 1.5 release intervals rather than ticks;
+ * they are set when a pipe is configured, so set release_us first */
+#define DN_RELEASE_GRAIN_NS	DN_RELEASE_NS
 extern int dn_release_us;	/* net.inet.ip.dummynet.release_us, 0: the tick */
 
 /* the longest a due packet waits for release, in us */
